# The container's schedule, run by supercronic (see Dockerfile). Times are in TZ, which the image sets to
# America/Denver, as equity-watch's does, so every time in these services is in one zone. New York and
# Denver change their clocks on the same dates, so these stay at the same point in the session all year:
# 7:40 is ten minutes after the open, 13:20 is forty minutes before the close.
#
# Four scans a weekday. Each saves its whole ranked result to /data/runs, which is the log `validate`
# needs, then rebuilds the report and publishes it. A spread listed on several runs counts once, at its
# first listing. Edit an expression and rebuild.
#
# There is no holiday calendar. A scan on a market holiday runs against the last session's quotes
# and saves a run that repeats the day before; harmless to `validate`, but the published report
# will say it ran.
#
# The 15-minute line is only the heartbeat the healthcheck reads (healthcheck.sh): the scans are
# too far apart for their own timestamp to say the scheduler is alive.
*/15 * * * * touch /tmp/alive
40 7 * * 1-5 /app/docker/run-scan.sh
30 9,11 * * 1-5 /app/docker/run-scan.sh
20 13 * * 1-5 /app/docker/run-scan.sh
